// @check
// @error print of a union value (K | i32) is type-valid but not yet supported by codegen
// CONTRACT (must-error): the ALIAS spelling of the mixed union. `K`'s members flatten into
// sibling literal members of the union, so the gate sees three literals and a scalar — two
// distinct softened bases, hence the box.
//
// The alias form matters on its own because the emit NAME keeps `K` un-softened in some
// positions (a closure RESULT registers the alias atom), which is why the softening lives in
// the print gate's own leaf walk and not in `retAtomKindOf` — softening there mis-reps
// `closures/closure-result-litunion-arm-union.vl`. Before D-LITPRINT: invalid wasm.
type K = "a" | "b"
const v: K | i32 = 3
print(v)
